# From "Orientation" (Wave I - Discovery, CD1-1), the tape that establishes
# Focus 3. It counts three to one, not ten to one: the ten-point system has
# not been used, so there is no Focus 10 to be counted out of. Kept separate
# from return.gws's ten-count, return-twelve.gws's twelve-count and
# return-one.gws's learned instant exit.

@segment   return-three
@title     Ending — Focus 3 to Waking
@levels    F3
@fixed
@continuous-exit
@duration  ~1m20s

say I'm going to count now from three to one.
pause 4
say And when I reach the count of one, all of your five physical senses will be operating clearly, cleanly, sharply, and beautifully.
pause 3
say You'll be completely wide awake, both physically and mentally, and feel completely refreshed, and feel better in every way, all when I reach the count of one.
pause 5
say I'm going to count now.
pause 4
say Three.
pause 3
say Two.
pause 4
say Your senses are waking up. All of your physical senses are waking up, and becoming more and more aware.
pause 4
say When I reach the count of one, all of your five physical senses will be operating clearly, cleanly, sharply, and beautifully.
pause 3
say You'll be completely wide awake, both physically and mentally, and be completely refreshed.
pause 4
say All when I reach the count of one.
pause 4
say One. Wake up.
pause 3
say Open your eyes. Stretch your arms and legs. Breathe deeply.
pause 6
say And this completes the exercise.
pause 4
